The provider is recovered from the work authored by Mhyzb / @Irisuko in the
archived vLLM-HUST repositories. Exact commits and file hashes are listed in
PROVENANCE.md.

The implementation describes itself as a clean-room implementation of the
observable PyramidKV selection semantics. Algorithm and comparison references
include:

  PyramidKV: Dynamic KV Cache Compression based on Pyramidal Information
  Funneling, arXiv:2406.02069
  https://arxiv.org/abs/2406.02069

  Zefan-Cai/KVCache-Factory (MIT License)
  https://github.com/Zefan-Cai/KVCache-Factory

  Irisuko/KVCache-Factory-Ascend commit
  fc6f8f4c3d8ca7a1849a2ef67ff5fca8d285a6f0 (MIT-licensed fork)
  https://github.com/Irisuko/KVCache-Factory-Ascend/commit/fc6f8f4c3d8ca7a1849a2ef67ff5fca8d285a6f0

No Hugging Face model patches, CUDA kernels, Triton kernels, or custom kernels
from those repositories are included in this package. Referenced projects keep
their own copyright and license terms.

The standalone adapter in src/vllm_ascend_pyramidkv/adapter and its lifecycle
regression tests are adapted from vLLM-HUST/vllm-ascend-kvcompress-hust,
commit f33785844be5bff7716c9464dd8444ef0b4b05e9, licensed Apache-2.0.
Copyright HUST CGCL, Sichen Liu and the contributing vLLM-HUST authors.
The local adaptation binds PyramidKV directly and excludes TriAttention's
method registry, calibration, scoring and compression kernels.

The plugin-owned Qwen GDN output Triton kernel is adapted from the
vLLM-Ascend-HUST flash-linear-attention-derived chunk output kernel.
Copyright (c) 2023-2025 Songlin Yang and Yu Zhang and vLLM contributors.
The original MIT notice is retained in LICENSES/flash-linear-attention-MIT.txt.
This supplies missing Qwen GDN registration only; no AscendC/Catlass binaries
are redistributed.
